Daemons joins the caret column
=============================

Daemons was the one plural entry without a caret, so its icon started ~26px further left than
Projects, Artifacts, Cron jobs and Tools & skills, and the column read as a mistake in the alignment.

It is a group now, expanding to the services it checks: streaming speech, Kokoro voice, the embedding
index, the model server, vision and input injection. Same icon column, same indent, same behaviour as
the other four.

Also here: `navigationButton` takes the page it belongs to and sets `aria-current` plus the active
class itself, so the rail's state is not left to whichever call site remembered to pass a class.

Correction worth recording: I first reported that the active rail never fired. It does — the plain nav
rows pass `state.page === page ? "active" : ""` already. The window I measured happened to be on "New
instance", which is a button of its own rather than a nav row, so no row was active and none should
have been. The rail was fine; the column was not.
